msgstr ""
"**[Tõrkeotsing](troubleshooting.md)** — kui miski on punane, alusta siit."

#: src/introduction.md:30
msgid ""
"**[Command reference](reference.md)** — every command and flag, generated "
"from the binary itself."
msgstr ""
"**[Käskude viide](reference.md)** — iga käsk ja lipp, genereeritud otse "
"binaarfailist endast."

#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "Märkus väljundi kohta"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat on ehitatud nii, et seda oleks meeldiv kasutada _ja_ turvaline "
"skriptida. Sõbralikud detailid — 🐐 kui kõik on roheline, vihje su järgmise "
"sammu kohta — ilmuvad ainult interaktiivses terminalis. Suuna goat skripti "
"või küsi `--json` ning saad puhta, stabiilse, masinloetava väljundi, milles "
"pole midagi dekoratiivset ees. Sea `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` ja isegi interaktiivsed "
"uhkeldused jäävad vait."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Alustamiseks ei ole vaja profiili, komplekti ega võrku. goatiga on kaasas "
"liivakast, et saaksid õppida tegevuse kaudu, turvaliselt."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Ütle tere"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — ütleb `lo` fabricule kui `default` teemal `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     võttis teema `hello/default` vastu (simuleeritud)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     suunas `lo` teemale `hello/default` üle WireGuard "
"P2P tee (simuleeritud)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber su tellija sai `lo` kätte — edasi-tagasi-reis "
"lõpetatud (simuleeritud)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: esimene sõnum, mis kunagi võrgu kaudu saadeti (ARPANET, 29. okt "
"1969) — nad trükkisid \"LOGIN\" ja ühendus kukkus pärast kahte tähte kokku.\n"
"edasi-tagasi-reis lõpetatud.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` avaldab sõnumi, tellib selle ja jälgib, kuidas see tagasi tuleb "
"— jutustades iga hüppe, mille andmed läbisid. Liivakastis on need hüpped "
"simuleeritud; päris keskkonna vastu on need päris. Mõlemal juhul, kui see "
"ütleb _round-trip complete_, tead, et tee töötab algusest lõpuni."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr "Sõnum on `lo` meelega — esimene asi, mis kunagi võrgu kaudu saadeti."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Tee ringkäik"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` on omas tempos läbitav käed-küljes ringkäik — mõtle sellest kui "
"`vimtutor`-ist fabricu jaoks. Kaheksa lühikest õppetundi viivad sind \"mis "
"see on\" juurest avaldamiseni, tellimiseni, diagnoosimiseni ja aluskihi "
"kaskaadi lugemiseni. Vaikimisi käib see liivakastis, salvestab su koha ning "
"saad igal ajal peatuda ja jätkata:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Ühenda päris keskkond"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Kui sulle on väljastatud liitumis-**komplekt** (`.cbor` fail su "
"identiteediga), võtab viisard siit üle:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` on sõbralik esiuks — see tuvastab, kas oled seadistatud, laseb "
"sul valida liivakasti või päris keskkonna, tõestab, et see töötab, ja suunab "
"sind õpetaja juurde. `goat doctor` käivitab seejärel astmelise "
"kättesaadavuskontrolli (mesh → router → sertifikaat → portaal) ja kui midagi "
"on valesti, ütleb täpselt, mida parandada."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr "Kui kõik doctori sammud läbivad, näed väikest 🐐 — oled fabricul."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Kuhu edasi"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr "Ideed on uued? Loe **[Kuidas fabric töötab](concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Valmis asju tegema? Hüppa **[Igapäevaste ülesannete](everyday.md)** juurde."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Midagi ei tööta? **[Tõrkeotsing](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"Sa saad goati produktiivselt kasutada vaid kolme ideega: **identiteet**, "
"**teemad** ja **vahendaja puudumine**. Siin nad on."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "Mesh, millega liitud identiteedi abil"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"Fabric on iseparanev mesh. Sõlmed ühenduvad üksteisega **otse** üle "
"krüpteeritud WireGuard tunnelite — kui oled liitunud, ei kulge su andmed "
"läbi keskserveri ja su ühendused jäävad püsima nii halduskihi katkestuse kui "
"ka ebakindla ülesvoolu korral."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Sa liitud **identiteediga**: liitumis-_komplektiga_, mis kannab su "
"sertifikaati, juurdepääsutõendit ja teadmist, kus fabric asub. Fabric lubab "
"sind sisse selle järgi, _kes sa oled_, mitte jagatud parooli järgi. `goat "
"profile init <bundle.cbor>` paigaldab selle identiteedi; sa võid hoida mitut "
"erinevate _kontekstide_ all ja nende vahel vahetada."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Teemad: avalda ja telli"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Andmed liiguvad **teemadel** — kaldkriipsudega eraldatud teed nagu `acme/"
"radar1/tracks`. Mudel on avalda/telli:"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr "**Avalda** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) kirjutab väärtuse teemasse."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Telli** (`goat sub <topic>`) võtab vastu iga sinna avaldatud väärtuse "
"reaalajas, niikaua kui sul on lubatud seda lugeda."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"Teema on lihtsalt nimi; sa lood selle (`goat topic create`), avaldad sinna "
"ja igaüks, kellel on luba, saab tellida. `goat hello` on lihtsalt avaldamine "
"ja tellimine kokku ühendatud, et saaksid jälgida, kuidas väärtus teeb edasi-"
"tagasi-reisi."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Vahendaja puudub — ja miks see loeb"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Andmetee keskel ei istu **mingit keskvahendajat**. Kui sa avaldad, voolab "
"väärtus üle meshi otse sõlmedele, kes selle on tellinud. See on tahtlik: see "
"kõrvaldab ainsa pudelikaela ja ainsa tõrkepunkti, mis vahendaja oleks."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"Praktiline tagajärg: **lugemine on lai, kirjutamine on piir.** Teema "
"_lugemise_ võimalus on disainilt lubav; sinna _kirjutamist_ reguleerib su "
"identiteet. Seega tabad harva üllatust selle osas, mida saad tellida, ning "
"avaldatu terviklikkus on ankurdatud selle juurde, kes selle avaldas."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Liivakast vs. päris"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Kõigel ülaltoodul on ustav **protsessisisene simulatsioon** — liivakast. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` ja `goat tutor` harjutavad "
"samu kujundeid (teema, avaldamine, edasi-tagasi-reis, otsus) ilma võrgu ja "
"identiteedita, nii et saad mudelit õppida enne, kui puudutad päris fabricut. "
"Liivakast ütleb seda alati `◇ SANDBOX` bänneriga ega kirjuta ega loe kunagi "
"päris meshist."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Kui lülitud päris keskkonnale, _käsud ei muutu_ — muutub ainult see, mis on "
"taustal."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Tahad sügavamat arhitektuuri (relee varuvariant, juurdepääsumudel, "
"auditijälg)? Küsi oma goat-administraatorilt disainiviiteid — see juhend "
"keskendub CLI kasutamisele."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Käsud, mille järele sa tegelikult haarad, kiirete retseptidena. Lisa ükskõik "
"millisele neist `--help`, et näha kõiki lippe, või vaata **[Käskude viidet]"
"(reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Kontrolli, et oled ühendatud"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` on su esimene peatus alati, kui miski tundub valesti — iga "
"ebaõnnestuv samm trükib konkreetse parandussoovituse. Kui kõik on roheline, "
"annavad mõlemad käsud selge \"kõik korras\" märguande."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Avalda ja telli"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # jälgi teemat reaalajas (Ctrl-C "
"peatamiseks)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # terve alampuu\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # avalda kandevoog\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr "Tahad näha lainetust, mille avaldamine vallandab? Lisa `--narrate`:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Töö teemadega"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # loetle teemad\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # süvene organisatsiooni/"
"eesliitesse\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # ühe teema täielik kirje\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Pärast teema loomist suunab goat sind loomuliku järgmise sammu poole (jälgi "
"seda või avalda sinna)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "Diagnoosi probleem"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` tagastab leiud ja iga jaoks lahenduse — mis on valesti ja mida "
"sellega teha."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skriptimine"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"Iga käsk, mis trükib inimvaate, pakub ka `--json` stabiilse, masinloetava "
"jaoks. JSON-kuju ei kanna kunagi bännereid, vihjeid ega uhkeldusi ning selle "
"kuju ja su väljumiskood jäävad väljalasete ja keelte lõikes muutumatuks:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr "See on leping: **sõbralik terminalis, puhas torus.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"Üks hoiatus: `goat status` avab igal käivitusel ruuteris päris seansi, seega on see kontroll, mille käivitad siis, kui tahad vastust, mitte midagi, mida taimerist küsitleda. Ajalise trendi jaoks kasuta `goat health` või `goat top`, mis loevad seda, mida goatnet juba avaldab."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat on üks iseseisev binaarfail — pole käituskeskkonda ega sõltuvusi. Seda "
"serveeritakse mesh-siseselt aadressilt `get.<your-goatnet>` (oled juba "
"meshil, kui suudad seda lugeda) ning siinne versioon vastab alati "
"binaarfailile, mida see pind serveerib."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Kiire paigaldus"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Veendu, et `~/.local/bin` on su `PATH`-is."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"Iga alamkäsk töötab Windowsis peale `goat client` (kohalik tunneli deemon), "
"mis on ainult Linuxi/macOS-i jaoks."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Kontrolli allalaadimist (soovituslik)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"Allalaadimispind avaldab iga binaari kohta `*.sha256` ja koond-`SHA256SUMS`. "
"Kõrge kindlusega paigalduseks kontrolli enne käivitamist:"

#: src/install.md:33
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""

#: src/install.md:34
msgid "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"
msgstr "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"

